# Vercel + Next.js serverless packaging.
#
# pnpm's default ("isolated") node_modules layout is symlink-based. On Vercel
# that breaks two things at once:
#
#   1. The build can fail with
#      "The framework produced an invalid deployment package for a Serverless
#       Function. Typically this means that the framework produces files in
#       symlinked directories."
#   2. node-file-trace cannot statically resolve requires that pass through the
#      symlinked store, so `next/dist/compiled/source-map` gets dropped from the
#      serverless bundle. Every server-rendered route then dies at runtime with
#      "Cannot find module 'next/dist/compiled/source-map'" (HTTP 500), while
#      statically prerendered pages keep working because they never invoke a
#      function. Upstream: vercel/next.js#83248.
#
# A hoisted layout emits real directories instead of symlinks, which fixes the
# packaging error and lets the tracer see the full `next` package. The module
# is still force-included via `outputFileTracingIncludes` in app/next.config.ts.
node-linker=hoisted
